WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.660
This is our timeline of the history of Genetics.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.931
So far, we have covered the important milestones

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.140
up to this point.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.236
Yes, we have taken a look at the work of Gregor

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.100
Mendel, followed by the work of Sutton and

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.080
Boveri.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.340
This was the Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.300
Later, it was Thomas Hunt Morgan who put forth

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.550
his work on the common fruit fly and achieved

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:30.700
another milestone.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.940
Now comes the next one!

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.160
After Morgan gave an experimental evidence

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:39.550
of the fact that genes for the traits are

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.509
present on the chromosomes, the scientific

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:45.890
world then got together to find out what exactly

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.480
makes up these genes and chromosomes.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.020
In other words, the chemical nature of this

00:00:52.028 --> 00:00:54.810
genetic material is what everyone was curious

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.920
to know about!

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.500
In the same era, a British bacteriologist

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.420
was busy handling his pneumococcal strains.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.780
They are nothing but the bacteria named Streptococcus

00:01:06.789 --> 00:01:09.490
pneumoniae, which are the causative agents

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.560
of pneumococcal infections.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:15.060
Fredrick Griffith found that there is some

00:01:15.062 --> 00:01:17.670
factor that helps TRANSFORM one bacterial

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.920
type into the other.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:23.820
Let us have a look at his remarkable experiment!

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.500
To begin with, we need to get introduced to

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.120
the two types of pneumococcal strains.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.260
This one is a smooth strain, denoted as the “S” strain.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.320
And this one is a rough strain, denoted as the “R” strain.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.940
Why are they named so?

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:43.419
Well, this smooth strain as we can see, has

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.280
a smooth outer surface.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:48.240
It’s the capsule around the cell wall which

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.180
protects it from various threats.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.879
The presence of this capsule makes the strain

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.740
virulent, or strongly infectious to be precise!

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.580
The absence of such a smooth coat makes this

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.580
strain avirulent, or non-infectious to be

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:05.220
precise!

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.220
Why is the R strain avirulent you may ask...

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:12.554
It’s the absence of the capsule which makes

00:02:12.554 --> 00:02:14.780
it susceptible to the immune cells of the

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.240
host’s body!

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.780
Now getting back to Griffith’s work, let

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.340
us see what experiment he exactly performed…

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.720
He first injected a mouse with the “S”

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.940
strain, which is the smooth strain of pneumococci.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.660
As expected, the mouse died.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.760
Similarly, on injecting another mouse with

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.720
a rough strain, the mouse survived.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.600
This was pretty much anticipated by him because

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.240
the “Rough” strain is usually the avirulent

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:44.900
one.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:46.920
What was done next?

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.985
Now the third mouse was injected with the

00:02:49.985 --> 00:02:52.900
“S” strain, but AFTER the bacteria were

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.019
heat killed.

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:56.711
That means he heated the ‘S’ strain to

00:02:56.711 --> 00:03:00.040
extreme temperatures, which killed the virulent

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.069
strain and made it ineffective.

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:06.230
So the injected mouse survived!

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:08.599
Now comes the last part!

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:10.945
This time Griffith injected a mouse with a

00:03:10.945 --> 00:03:13.459
mixture of both, rough strain and heat killed

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.980
smooth strain.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.297
Yes, a mixture of the rough strain and the

00:03:19.297 --> 00:03:21.969
HEAT KILLED smooth strain.

00:03:21.969 --> 00:03:24.249
What do you think would have happened?

00:03:24.249 --> 00:03:26.936
Most of us would expect the mouse to survive

00:03:26.936 --> 00:03:29.439
because both are individually ineffective

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:30.930
or avirulent.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:35.776
However, to his astonishment, the mouse did

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:36.980
not survive!

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.360
How did this happen?

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.739
And what do you think Griffith concluded?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.080
With this, he concluded that there was SOMETHING

00:03:44.088 --> 00:03:46.739
from the “S” strain that was PASSED ON

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:50.480
to the “R” strain, resulting it to turn “Virulent”.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.580
Also, do you know what he recovered from the

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.500
body of the mouse?

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.640
He recovered live “S” strain.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.240
Surprising isn’t it?

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.300
This further confirmed that the “R” strain

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.660
was transformed into the virulent “S”

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:06.240
strain.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.020
He named the ”transforming factor” as

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.700
the “TRANSFORMATION PRINCIPLE”.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.960
He did not really know what exactly this was,

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.140
and hence named it just the “transformation

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:17.840
principle”.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:22.420
But he predicted that this could be the genetic material.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.260
Was this really the genetic material?

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.200
Or was it something else?

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.180
Let us find that out in the next part!

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.000
Imagine we are given a bag full of flowers.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.760
And we are told that there is one flower which

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.600
has the “Midas effect”.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.660
Anything that the flower touches, gets transformed into

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:47.460
gold!

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:51.800
But how will we find out which flower is the special one?

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:54.500
All the flowers look more or less the same!

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.271
Well, the only thing we can do is make all

00:04:57.271 --> 00:04:59.250
the flowers touch some object.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.030
Isn’t that right?

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.060
So examining every individual flower is the

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.580
only option we have!

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.940
The story was similar in the case of

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.320
“TRANSFORMATION

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:10.460
PRINCIPLE”.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.237
After Griffith concluded his experiment on

00:05:13.237 --> 00:05:15.371
the bacteria named Streptococcus pneumoniae,

00:05:15.371 --> 00:05:18.777
the science world was now curious to know

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.340
more about the transformation principle.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.720
Finding the answers was not a piece of cake though!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.382
It was almost two decades later that three

00:05:28.382 --> 00:05:31.360
scientists figured out what this transformation

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.860
principle was!

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:35.431
They tried finding out its chemical nature

00:05:35.431 --> 00:05:38.430
by testing every single component of the virulent

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:39.680
bacterial strain.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.716
Let us move a step ahead in the timeline and

00:05:42.716 --> 00:05:45.960
understand the interesting experiment performed

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.510
by Avery, MacLeod and McCarty around the year 1944.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.100
The three scientists were quite fascinated

00:05:54.103 --> 00:05:55.900
with Griffith’s work.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.400
Just like others, even they were curious to

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.560
know what the transformation principle was!

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.020
So they thought of continuing the same experiment

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.440
with better research!

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:09.000
Griffith concluded his experiment by inferring

00:06:09.002 --> 00:06:11.450
that there is some “factor” that is passed

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:14.100
from the heat killed virulent strain to the

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.500
rough strain which is avirulent.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:19.680
This factor transforms the avirulent strain

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.380
to the virulent type.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.510
So the three scientists thought of planning

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.780
the experiment by targeting the heat killed

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.020
smooth strain.

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:31.380
Just like our bag filled with flowers, the

00:06:31.384 --> 00:06:34.340
smooth strain cells had various chemical components

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:35.200
in them.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.660
And just like how we had to examine the touch

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:41.440
of individual flowers, the scientists mixed

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.340
every single chemical component individually

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.760
with the rough strain.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.680
So let’s say this smooth strain cell had

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.680
these 4 components A, B, C and D in it.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.760
They mixed the component “A” with the

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.720
rough strain and injected it in a live mouse.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.800
Similarly, they mixed all the other components

00:07:01.808 --> 00:07:04.780
individually with the rough strains and injected

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:07.280
the mixtures in different mice.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:10.398
What they found at the end was, only one of

00:07:10.398 --> 00:07:12.970
those components among all, was effective

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:16.080
in transforming the rough strain.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.120
It was the case in which the mouse died.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.880
The conclusion was that component “D”

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.600
transformed the “R” strain!

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.000
They isolated this component from the heat

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.760
killed strain and tested it further.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.120
On chemical analysis they could figure out

00:07:34.123 --> 00:07:37.020
that the molecules had a chemical composition

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.400
similar to that of DNA.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:44.340
Deoxyribonucleic Acid, abbreviated as DNA,

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.760
was known to people by this time.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:49.770
But it was not given much importance.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:52.300
Nobody assumed that it could be such a vital

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.200
part of the cell.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.900
In fact, people thought that “PROTEINS”

00:07:55.907 --> 00:07:56.940
made up the cells.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:59.820
And it was also believed that proteins make

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.680
up the GENETIC material.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.600
So this experiment was a huge breakthrough

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:05.620
in genetics!

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.980
Many tests were carried out to investigate

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.200
this further and the chemical composition

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:14.700
of this Transformation principle was found.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.900
It had components in the ratio that were found

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.480
in the DNA molecules.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.940
So to FURTHER understand its nature, this

00:08:22.945 --> 00:08:25.670
component was tested using chemicals that

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.480
break down the constituents.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:32.080
For example, certain enzymes like protease

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.100
degrade proteins.

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:37.080
Use of such chemicals help us identify the

00:08:37.099 --> 00:08:39.750
constituents in a given sample as they will

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:42.200
degrade specific molecules only.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:46.053
So in this case, the chemicals used to degrade

00:08:46.053 --> 00:08:48.730
DNA were used along with others and it was

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:51.480
found that the chemicals successfully broke

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.900
down the molecules.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:56.460
It implied that the molecules were that of DNA.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.460
This chemical analysis helped in understanding

00:09:00.476 --> 00:09:02.939
that the “Transformation Principle” was

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.790
nothing else but DNA.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.160
But this wasn’t easily accepted as a fact!

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.337
A few years later, another experiment helped

00:09:11.337 --> 00:09:14.360
confirm the fact that it is indeed the DNA

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:16.083
which is the transformation principle

00:09:17.149 --> 00:09:19.645
Let us find out more about the experiment

00:09:19.645 --> 00:09:20.680
in the next part!

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:23.312
Until then, do not forget to subscribe to

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:25.680
our channel in order to get notified about

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:26.820
our latest uploads!

